DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     zzvviieeww is the window server and desktop of the COHERENT GUI
     on the hi-res (bitmap) display.  It loads the display driver
     /ddrrvv/hhrr and the pseudo-terminal driver /ddrrvv/ppttyy, takes over
     the screen and keyboard, loads the fonts, reads the applica-
     tion catalog, and runs the desktop start-up script - which
     normally starts the dock zzddoocckk, the icon bar along the top
     of the screen.  The server itself draws no icons: it manages
     windows, the way a kernel manages processes, and leaves the
     desktop's furnishing to the dock, its replaceable shell.  It
     takes no arguments.  At boot, /eettcc/rrcc starts it when the
     file /eettcc/wwgguuii exists - create that file to enable the GUI;
     it can equally be started by hand from the console: zzvviieeww &.

     The dock shows one icon per catalog application, always -
     see zzddoocckk for its conventions (left click launches or
     switches, middle click starts another copy of a multi-
     instance application).  Every window has a 3-button mouse
     and follows the same conventions:

